# ===========================================================================
#  source_fov_vision600.mac -- uniform box source filling the Vision 600 FOV.
#
#  The Vision 600 counterpart of source.mac. Same idea: fill the field of view
#  with a uniform back-to-back source so that
#
#      sensitivity(voxel) = detected coincidences / emitted annihilations
#
#  can be measured per voxel from the KNOWN annihilation position.
#
#  FOV = a 256 mm CUBE (+-128 mm), not the panel scanner's 400 mm.
#    * axially that is the ring itself: crystal centres span z = +-128.77 mm,
#      so there is no sensitivity to measure beyond it;
#    * transaxially +-128 mm comfortably contains the 224 mm reconstruction
#      grid (+-112 mm), so the map covers every reconstructed voxel with no
#      extrapolation.
#  A cube is required because scripts/sensitivity.py bins the same half-width
#  on all three axes (--fov sets the side).
#
#  ACTIVITY is an alias so the driver can trade activity against duration;
#  keep it modest so randoms stay negligible (they are removed anyway by
#  requiring eventID1 == eventID2, but they cost simulation time).
# ===========================================================================

/gate/source/addSource fov
/gate/source/fov/setActivity {ACTIVITY} becquerel
/gate/source/fov/setType backtoback

/gate/source/fov/gps/particle gamma
/gate/source/fov/gps/ene/type Mono
/gate/source/fov/gps/ene/mono 0.511 MeV

/gate/source/fov/gps/type Volume
/gate/source/fov/gps/shape Para
/gate/source/fov/gps/halfx 128. mm
/gate/source/fov/gps/halfy 128. mm
/gate/source/fov/gps/halfz 128. mm
/gate/source/fov/gps/paralp 0. deg
/gate/source/fov/gps/parthe 0. deg
/gate/source/fov/gps/parphi 0. deg
/gate/source/fov/gps/centre 0. 0. 0. mm

/gate/source/fov/gps/angtype iso
/gate/source/fov/gps/mintheta 0. deg
/gate/source/fov/gps/maxtheta 180. deg
/gate/source/fov/gps/minphi 0. deg
/gate/source/fov/gps/maxphi 360. deg

/gate/source/list
